Subject: ps2xRuntime: external presentation (the game's renderer presents, raylib only polls)

For the Rule of Rose port's PCSX2 GS (renderer plan step 2): PCSX2 presents into a child window of the raylib window.
setExternalPresentation(init, loop, shutdown, user): init at the start of run(), then each main-loop iteration only
PollInputEvents + loop + the close check + a 4 ms sleep instead of UploadFrame/BeginDrawing/EndDrawing, and shutdown
after the game thread has joined, before CloseWindow (the child window and its swap chain go first).

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime.h
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime.h
@@ -307,6 +307,16 @@
                              DebugUiCallback shutdownCallback,
                              void *userData);
 
+    // Presentation by the game's own renderer (e.g. a GS presenting into a child window): with a loop callback set,
+    // the main loop keeps polling input and the close request but draws nothing. All three run on the main (window)
+    // thread: init in run() before the game thread starts (the window exists), loop once per iteration (about 250 Hz),
+    // shutdown after the game thread has stopped and before CloseWindow. Set before run() (a game override may).
+    using ExternalPresentationCallback = void (*)(PS2Runtime &runtime, void *userData);
+    void setExternalPresentation(ExternalPresentationCallback initCallback,
+                                 ExternalPresentationCallback loopCallback,
+                                 ExternalPresentationCallback shutdownCallback,
+                                 void *userData);
